  // rendered bytes. Then real opencode / hermes-agent / turnstone clients are planned and applied; the snapshots compare
  // the files each side wrote byte for byte (roots are the harness's existing home/project and home/project2, so their
  // files do not overlap the e2e clients'; the turnstone console is a closed port). (Needs WS-B1 on the Rust side.)
